Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:09:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 55/57] drama: the silence guard also ends a reply that
 collapses into its voice's noise floor

A reply can collapse into a steady hum instead of digital silence, whose frames keep rising above -60 dBFS, so the run kept restarting and the reply ended stop. A frame is now silent below -40 dBFS. Replayed over 278 renders of the built-in and model-invented voices, the guard ends all 11 collapses 10 s after each began (one of them missed at -60 dBFS) and none of the other 267; the recovering 7.4 s stall is 7.5 s at the new floor.
